This is an automated test suite for ArduPilot

Where tests live
================

Each vehicle test suite has a test root directory: ArduCopter_Tests,
Helicopter_Tests, ArduPlane_Tests, QuadPlane_Tests, ArduRover_Tests,
BalanceBot_Tests, Sailboat_Tests, ArduSub_Tests, Blimp_Tests and
AntennaTracker_Tests.  Each test has a directory of its own in its root,
holding the test and any missions, fences, scripts or other files it
uses:

  ArduCopter_Tests/AuxFunctionsInMission/AuxFunctionsInMission.py
  ArduCopter_Tests/AuxFunctionsInMission/aux_functions.txt

The tests are found by test_discovery.py; there is no list to add them
to.  Tests defined in vehicle_test_suite.py, which run on every vehicle,
are still listed in TestSuite.tests().

Adding a test
=============

Create <root>/<Name>/<Name>.py:

  '''
  Copter autotest: MyNewTest

  AP_FLAKE8_CLEAN
  '''

  from test_discovery import TestGroup
  from test_discovery import testcase


  class MyNewTest(TestGroup):
      @testcase(bucket="CopterTests1c")
      def MyNewTest(self):
          '''one-line description of what is tested'''
          self.takeoff(10, mode="LOITER")
          ...

The methods run as methods of the vehicle's test suite, so "self" gives
access to every helper in vehicle_test_suite.py and the vehicle's test
file.  Files loaded with load_mission(), load_fence() and friends are
looked for in the test's directory.

bucket names the CI job running the test: an entry in tester_class_map
in autotest.py without its "test." prefix (CopterTests1a, PlaneTests1b,
QuadPlaneTests1c, Rover, Sub, Helicopter...).  Pick the bucket with the
shortest run time; a list of buckets runs the test in each.  @testcase
also takes attempts, speedup, kwargs and disabled (a reason; the test
is then skipped).

Tests sharing code form a family in one directory: the helper is a
method of the TestGroup class without @testcase, and every test's name
starts with the directory name (ArduPlane_Tests/Deadreckoning holds
Deadreckoning and DeadreckoningNoAirSpeed).  Helpers used by tests in
several directories belong on the vehicle's test suite class.

Do not use zero-argument super() in a TestGroup: the methods are
installed onto the suite class, so name it, e.g.
super(AutoTestBalanceBot, self).DriveRTL().

Run a test with, e.g.:

  Tools/autotest/autotest.py build.Copter test.Copter.MyNewTest

History of moved tests
======================

The tests used to be methods in arducopter.py, arduplane.py and the
other vehicle files, and were moved into their directories unchanged.
To follow a test's lines back past that move use

  git blame --minimal -C Tools/autotest/ArduPlane_Tests/Deadreckoning/Deadreckoning.py

(both options are needed), or read the old file's history from a
commit before the move:

  git log -L '/def Deadreckoning(self)/,+3:Tools/autotest/arduplane.py' <commit>

GitHub's blame view and "git log --follow" do not cross the move.
